Cheren: {VAR 0100 0000}, stop!{VAR BE01}
You've got a Bolt Badge...
I've got a Bolt Badge...{VAR BE01}
Let's test who's stronger--you or me!
This time, I'm going to win!{VAR BE01}

Elesa: Oh, you two are friends...{VAR BE01}
That's nice, how you're helping each
other get better by competing.{VAR BE01}

Cheren: Champion?!{VAR BE01}
Why would the Champion be
goofing off in a place like this?{VAR BE01}

Alder: I heard that remark.
You're quite a judgmental young person,{VAR BE00}
are you not?{VAR BE01}
My name is Alder. I'm the Unova
Pokémon League's Champion.{VAR BE01}
Pleased to make your acquaintance.{VAR BE01}
For your information, I'm not
goofing off. I'm on a voyage.{VAR BE00}
I know every corner of Unova.{VAR BE01}

Cheren: Um. I'm Cheren, from
Nuvema Town.{VAR BE01}
My goal as a Trainer is to
become the Champion.{VAR BE01}

Alder: Hm. Traveling with a goal in mind
is a commendable thing.{VAR BE01}
And what do you plan to do
after becoming the Champion?{VAR BE01}

Cheren: What else is there other than
striving to become stronger?{VAR BE01}
The strongest Trainer--
that's the Champion.{VAR BE01}

Alder: Hmm. Becoming stronger...
Becoming stronger, you say...{VAR BE00}
Is that alone enough of a goal? Hmmm.{VAR BE01}
It's not that I'm trying to say your way
of thinking is wrong...{VAR BE01}

In my travels, I've helped many people
learn to love Pokémon. I think that's{VAR BE00}
important, too.{VAR BE01}
If you play with those children,
you might gain more of an understanding.{VAR BE01}
Will you two have a Pokémon battle
with those two?{VAR BE01}

Alder: Nicely done! You didn't win, but
that was a good battle. Your Pokémon{VAR BE00}
looked like they were having fun.{VAR BE01}

Young man, if there are people
like you who pursue strength,{VAR BE00}
there are also people who are{VAR BE00}
happy just being with Pokémon.{VAR BE01}
There are many different people
and many different answers.{VAR BE01}
When it comes to what a Champion
should be, you and I may hold differing{VAR BE00}
views, but so be it! Give it some thought.{VAR BE01}

Alder: It's tremendous that people and
Pokémon, each so different, can{VAR BE00}
acknowledge each other and be together!

It's me, Elesa.
Please lower the drawbridge.{VAR BE01}
I have a couple of Trainers here
who want to challenge you.{VAR BE01}
OK...
Thanks.{VAR BE01}

Elesa: I have a TV gig, so I've got to go.{VAR BE01}
The Gym Leader of the next town
may take some getting used to...{VAR BE00}
Do your best, both of you.{VAR BE01}

Cheren: What I am is a Trainer.{VAR BE01}
I prove I'm right by getting stronger
and winning in battle--{VAR BE00}
even against the Champion.{VAR BE01}

The drawbridge is raised right now
so ships can pass. You can't cross.{VAR BE01}
If you make a request to Driftveil's Gym
Leader, Clay, he could... Well, I'm not{VAR BE00}
sure how you'd reach him over there...{VAR BE01}
If you talk to Nimbasa City's Gym Leader,
Elesa, she might be able to do something.

The drawbridge is raised right now
so ships can pass. You can't cross.{VAR BE01}
If you make a request to Driftveil's Gym
Leader, Clay, he could... Well, I'm not{VAR BE00}
sure how you'd reach him over there...{VAR BE01}
If you talk to Nimbasa City's Gym Leader,
Elesa, she might be able to do something.{VAR BE01}

In battling you, I came to understand...{VAR BE01}
You're the best!
Here! This is for you!{VAR BE01}

If you want your Pokémon to
hold this Electric Guitar,{VAR BE00}
go to the Musical Theater!{VAR BE00}
Cooler than cool!

Cheren: Strength and strength alone
is what matters in this world.{VAR BE01}
So I believed, until I met Alder here.{VAR BE01}

But, winning in Pokémon battles
isn't all there is to life.{VAR BE01}
Once I learned that lesson, my eyes
were opened to many different things.{VAR BE01}

We all have our own brand of strength,
people and Pokémon both.{VAR BE01}
The strength to make our dreams
a reality, the strength to protect{VAR BE00}
what we hold most dear...{VAR BE01}

Why do I think this way now?
It's thanks to you, {VAR 0100 0000}...{VAR BE01}
And Bianca...
And Alder...{VAR BE01}
If only N could see this, too, someday.{VAR BE01}

I'm going to take a long, hard look
at myself on Victory Road.{VAR BE01}
I'm going to think about what I can do
and who I can become...{VAR BE01}
Visit me sometime, if you want.
We'll have a battle like old times.{VAR BE01}

